    {
      "id": "ha3fnrc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Ohm’s Law Triangle"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5dsil6q",
      "content": "The Ohm's Law triangle helps to remember formulas:<br></br>V at the top, I and R at the bottom.<br></br>Cover the quantity you want to find."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z9z0hgn",
      "content": "Derived formulas:"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Chapter 17 – Ohm’s Law and Electrical Measurements",
      "id": "1i5tsci"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3zq7fwu",
      "content": "I = V / R"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q3fu2w2",
      "content": "R = V / I"
    },
    {
      "id": "do43hnl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Electrical Resistance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w2l8cdx",
      "content": "Resistance is the opposition offered by a material to the flow of electric current."
    },
