      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Numerical Examples"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dfexjdk",
      "content": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eoxag50",
      "content": "A circuit has voltage 12 V and resistance 4 Ω.<br></br>Find current.<br></br>I = V / R = 12 / 4 = 3 A"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8y9lvfy",
      "content": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cltnktj",
      "content": "A circuit carries current 2 A and resistance is 5 Ω.<br></br>Find voltage.<br></br>V = I × R = 2 × 5 = 10 V"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Ideal Ammeter has ZERO resistance (connected in series); Ideal Voltmeter has INFINITE resistance (connected in parallel).",
        "If a wire is stretched to double its length, its new resistance becomes 4 times the original resistance.",
        "Galvanometer is converted into an Ammeter by connecting a low shunt resistance in parallel, and into a Voltmeter by connecting a high resistance in series."
      ],
      "id": "m5lcpoq"
    },
    {
